      "text": "Before everyone starts complaining about trump please pay attention to United States history and how many of our presidents bombed countries because you guys are looking real pathetic and seem really disingenuous when speaking \n\nLike&share Please\n\n@CryptoCollide @ace_report @Frankkiy @Hamnakedshorts @palmer1075 @vincefelice1234 @TintedVeil @ThatFroGirl50 @summerbylake @CarlDav38431620 @mhs_dogs @BigCFinancial @burnshorts123 @tommyb6101 @pman88888 @MBCHERT @toe_cramp @tonydito51 @radtdd99 \n@BAMinvestor @TradeMistress13 \n\nDuring his presidency (2009–2017), Barack Obama’s administration carried out military strikes—including drone attacks, airstrikes, and cruise missile launches—in at least seven countries, possibly eight, depending on definitions and sources. Here’s a breakdown:\n\n⸻\n\n🌍 Countries where Obama ordered military strikes\n•Afghanistan\nContinuation of the long-running war from the Bush era, with both manned aircraft and drones used in combat operations.  \n•Iraq\nAirstrikes began in August 2014 to combat ISIS and included both manned and unmanned aircraft.\n•Pakistan\nNumerous CIA drone strikes in tribal regions targeting militants—a major focus of Obama’s counterterror campaign.  \n•Somalia\nDrone and airstrikes against al‑Shabab militants; included special operations “signature” strikes.  \n•Yemen\nExtensive use of drones and some manned strikes targeting al‑Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula.\n•Libya\nTwo campaigns: 2011 NATO-led airstrikes under UN mandate (“Odyssey Dawn/Unified Protector”) and later 2015–16 U.S. strikes against ISIS.\n•Syria\nBeginning in September 2014, Obama authorized airstrikes—including cruise missiles and drone use—against ISIS and other militant targets.  \n\n⸻\n\n🕵️‍♂️ Possible additional country\n•Philippines\nSome reports indicate U.S. drone strikes occurred in 2012 targeting militants—though this remains less confirmed. If included, this would raise the total to eight countries.",
